     72 +New code notes:
     73 +
     74 +1. Line contingency loop now starts with a filtered snapshot query
     75 +
     76 +New code does this:
     77 +
     78 +    SQL = "SELECT * FROM Line WHERE InclAsCTG <> 0 AND start_date <= " & SqlDateLiteral(snapshotDate) & _
     79 +        " AND end_date > " & SqlDateLiteral(snapshotDate) & ";"
     80 +    Set Line = db.OpenRecordset(SQL, dbOpenSnapshot)
     81 +
     82 +What changed:
     83 +- Access now filters Line rows before VBA starts looping.
     84 +- Only included, active contingency lines are opened.
     85 +- dbOpenSnapshot is used because this writer is only reading the data.
     86 +- The old inside-loop InclAsCTG/date check is still kept as a backup check, but most rejected rows should never
          reach the loop now.
     87 +
     88 +
     89 +2. Queue dependency now uses the current Line row values
     90 +
     91 +New code does this:
     92 +
     93 +    QueueDependency = Not assessQueueDependencyValues(Line.Fields("Queue"), Line.Fields("NotQueue"), incNoIA, i
         gnoreAfterQueueNum)
     94 +
     95 +What changed:
     96 +- WritePwConFile no longer asks assessQueueDependency to query Line again by line_id.
     97 +- The current Line record already has Queue and NotQueue, so those values are passed directly.
     98 +- The old assessQueueDependency(lineID, ...) function is still kept because other code may call it.
     99 +- The old function now delegates into the new shared helper after reading Queue and NotQueue.
    100 +
