    102 +3. Branch lookup now opens SQL directly
    103 +
    104 +New code does this:
    105 +
    106 +    SQL = "SELECT * FROM Branch WHERE Branch.line_id = " & Line.Fields("line_id") & _
    107 +        " AND Branch.start_date <= " & SqlDateLiteral(snapshotDate) & _
    108 +        " AND " & SqlDateLiteral(snapshotDate) & " <= Branch.end_date;"
    109 +    Set filteredBranch = db.OpenRecordset(SQL, dbOpenSnapshot)
    110 +
    111 +What changed:
    112 +- No saved QueryDef is deleted.
    113 +- No saved QueryDef is created.
    114 +- Access opens the SQL directly as a temporary read-only snapshot.
    115 +- The Branch query now filters by line_id and active date before VBA loops the branches.
    116 +- The old inside-loop branch date check is still kept as a backup check.
    117 +- filteredBranch now closes even when the query returns no rows.
